Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: Veyon
Upstream-Contact: Tobias Junghans <tobydox@veyon.io>
Source: https://github.com/veyon/veyon/releases
Comment:
 The orig tarball is upstream's release tarball veyon-<version>-src.tar.bz2
 (which holds the git submodules), repacked by mk-origtargz without the
 Files-Excluded below, as Debian's veyon packages do: code and prebuilt
 binaries for MS Windows and Android (ddengine, interception, UltraVNC, NSIS),
 embedded copies of libraries that this package takes from the archive
 (libvncserver and x11vnc, libfakekey, the Qt HTTP Server module) and the
 Qt 5 copy of kldap, which a Qt 6 build does not use.
